StyleSmuggler mitigation (Sansec 2026-09-05): Magento's DI code scanners are
CLI-only. Unauthenticated RCE in every Magento / Adobe Commerce / Mage-OS release
up to 2.4.9 — attacker-controlled text reaches the email template filter, whose
{{block}} directive drives a method chain into the DI compiler's scanners, whose
include/require then executes a poisoned var/report or var/log file. These
scanners only ever run from bin/magento setup:di:compile, so reaching them over
HTTP is the attack and nothing else — the guard throws on any non-CLI SAPI.
Vendor patch pending (Adobe bulletin 2026-09-08); remove once it is in.

Source: https://github.com/disrex-group/stylesmuggler-mitigation
        patches/magento/magento2-base/stylesmuggler-di-scanner-guard.patch
Advisory: https://sansec.io/research/stylesmuggler

@package mage-os/magento2-base
@category security
@link https://sansec.io/research/stylesmuggler

